      "inputChecksum": "9f105a088a1812f0ef5e9f370cb6bf467f9da681c86cf77424c49e058f7a39fe",
      "summaryText": "This chunk explains how to index nearest neighbor queries that include a `WHERE` clause. It recommends creating an index on the filter column, noting that Postgres supports B-tree, hash, GiST, SP-GiST, GIN, and BRIN index types, and that multicolumn indexes can be created for multiple columns. It also discusses approximate indexes using HNSW, partial indexing for filtering by few distinct values, and partitioning for filtering by many different values.",
