      "inputChecksum": "e3a2537ca80e3db11845394e5cfd2c01f173cd9f63e27910ac5daf57a82bb19a",
      "summaryText": "Starting with pgvector 0.8.0, iterative index scans automatically scan more of an approximate index until enough results are found, stopping at `hnsw.max_scan_tuples` or `ivfflat.max_probes`. Scans can use strict ordering via `SET hnsw.iterative_scan = strict_order;` for exact distance order, or relaxed ordering via `SET hnsw.iterative_scan = relaxed_order;` or `SET ivfflat.iterative_scan = relaxed_order;` for better recall. With relaxed ordering, a materialized CTE can restore strict ordering, requiring `+ 0` for Postgres 17+, and distance filters should be placed outside the CTE for best performance.",
      "outputChecksum": "6cfe717b20fa4ede0cc45e3652ed022c6be87138fb3a2c41eec0ff22a8a3a946",
      "generationMetadata": {
