      "inputChecksum": "7be14541875e973a5880bb95bb0d6df4a7ac27e2891c707fe25a6e8c7424ff9d",
      "summaryText": "PostgreSQL 18 adds an asynchronous I/O subsystem that lets backends queue multiple read requests for more efficient sequential scans, bitmap heap scans, and vacuums, controlled by the server variables `io_method`, `io_combine_limit`, and `io_max_combine_limit`, while also enabling `effective_io_concurrency` and `maintenance_io_concurrency` values greater than zero on systems without `fadvise()` support and exposing used file handles through the new system view `pg_aios`. It also improves locking performance for queries accessing many relations, enhances hash joins and `GROUP BY` performance and reduces their memory usage, allows normal vacuums to freeze all-visible pages to reduce later full-relation freezing overhead via the `vacuum_max_eager_freeze_failure_rate` setting, and adds the `vacuum_truncate` server variable to control file truncation during `VACUUM`. Finally, the default values for `effective_io_concurrency` and `maintenance_io_concurrency` are increased to 16.",
      "outputChecksum": "92244bde64325ff6596ee488d3bc8ed47799b11a5e41750b0928c11a0d21fb85",
      "generationMetadata": {
        "backend": "llama-server",
