      "inputChecksum": "7ae69afb21e903dbfe7b7c9560dfdae1297c904be19144756c116e5527c0e92e",
      "summaryText": "PostgreSQL 18 introduces an asynchronous I/O (AIO) subsystem that improves performance of sequential scans, bitmap heap scans, vacuums, and other operations. It also adds features such as `pg_upgrade` retaining optimizer statistics, \"skip scan\" lookups for multicolumn B-tree indexes, the `uuidv7()` function for timestamp-ordered UUIDs, virtual generated columns (now the default), OAuth authentication support, `OLD` and `NEW` support in `RETURNING` clauses for INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and MERGE commands, and temporal constraints for PRIMARY KEY, UNIQUE, and FOREIGN KEY constraints. These new features are explained in more detail in the sections below.",
      "outputChecksum": "c79dd5ecf7f437493b279b1a03c13815a6e799fcd31c829567d9e37ace1f795b",
