      "inputChecksum": "dbd52954ab9b4e83c9d9cae36ac2ce5a7cfbb3a2445649fae0095b6c9839903b",
      "summaryText": "PostgreSQL 18 adds the `casefold()` function for more sophisticated case-insensitive matching that handles characters with multiple upper or lower case equivalents and conversions that change character counts. It also allows `MIN()`/`MAX()` aggregates on arrays and composite types, adds a `WEEK` option to `EXTRACT()` with improved negative value output for `EXTRACT(QUARTER ...)`, and adds roman numeral support to `to_number()` via the `RN` pattern. Additionally, it introduces the temporally sortable `uuidv7()` function with a `uuidv4()` alias, adds `crc32()` and `crc32c()` for CRC computation, adds `gamma()` and `lgamma()` math functions, and allows `=>` syntax for named cursor arguments in PL/pgSQL.",
