      "inputChecksum": "f591b3e8b5152ed1580c487d547b3d820eddf8da0e6863d38bf3c0476d8e4709",
      "summaryText": "In SvelteKit, data returned from a parent layout `load` function is accessible in child components through the `data` prop, allowing access to sibling data like `data.posts`. When multiple `load` functions return data with the same key, the last one wins, so a layout `load` returning `{ a: 1, b: 2 }` combined with a page `load` returning `{ b: 3, c: 4 }` results in `{ a: 1, b: 3, c: 4 }`.",
      "outputChecksum": "8137e44dba5da7defaae5aeaa02614d8ae8c1fa6a3784dd6c96ba471c92d2745",
